  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:immersive-workspaces",
  "domain": "spatial-computing",
  "definition": "Immersive workspaces are physical or virtual environments enhanced with spatial and extended-reality technologies\u2014including AR, VR, and mixed reality\u2014that allow users to interact intuitively with digital content and collaborators in three-dimensional space, fostering a strong sense of presence and engagement. They integrate spatial computing principles to support real-time manipulation of data, collaborative visualisation, immersive training, and seamless transitions between physical and digital environments. Immersive workspaces are increasingly deployed across corporate, industrial, and educational settings to support hybrid and remote collaboration at scale.",
